        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Avatar station error with the 2022 update.  To dismount players from avatar stations, the common way was to disable the game object the VRC_Station component was on.  If you toggle the collider, it doesn't dismount them.  There is no option to toggle the VRC_station component.\n\nCurrent 2022 behavior: if you disable the VRC_station gameobject it dismounts the player, but re-enabling the gameobject doesn't restore the station script or interaction with the collider so players can't use that station again.  This was fully functioning in 2019.  This functionality was used for things like portal toys and cart rides.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "654164fc1aaf69c4857f8046",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5f4c34d0995917085be1218d",
        "alias": "Zinc white Dragon",
        "aliasID": "65c2b40bed6eefce4ccc50d5",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/833c66b891dbc04385009d159c139d66.png",
        "created": "2020-08-30T23:22:56.091Z",
        "name": "CyanLaser",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62f2b3cf8f8367753b2f0",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-10-31T20:35:08.053Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64ebd6d8d1b9dd09809a3ae9",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 5
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Issue is still present in Live build 1373. This appears to be a combination of two bugs, one old and one new.\n\nOld bug: \n\nStations that are disabled on avatar upload never work. The fix originally was to ensure that stations were enabled on upload.\n\nNew bug:\n\nAnimators initialize and run before stations initialize. Animators that disable station GameObjects on the first frame will then cause stations to be disabled when the station initialization pass is run, causing them to never work on the avatar.\n\nA workaround that people have found is that if the user's avatar parameters have the station enabled when the avatar is loaded, then the station will work.  Having the player enable the station, and the other player hide/show to reload the player's avatar will temporarily fix it. Another workaround is to ensure that station gameobjects are enabled both in unity on upload and for the first few frames in your animators.\n\nPreferably, the solution would be that VRChat fixes the original bug that disabled stations never initialize properly, as this would fix more than just the bug introduced in the update a few months ago. I can only assume this is a bug caused by GetComponentsInChildren, without passing the \"true\" parameter to ensure that disabled components are also found.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
